# user.md — operator & agent identity (copy to user.md, fill in, gitignore the real file)

No PII or secrets in this template. The real `user.md` is gitignored, same as the recruiting/onboarding/people-ops packs' `user.md`.

## Agent identity

- **Agent name:** {AgentName} — pick something short, warm, obviously not a human name pretending to be human; must match `{{AGENT_NAME_TBD}}` once founder-approved (`agent.md`).
- **Agent mailbox:** TODO(gate) — not yet provisioned (`agent.md`).
- **Disclosure signature** (every employee-facing message, non-negotiable):
  ```
  — {AgentName}, OTPLESS's Culture & Growth agent (AI), working with Satyam
  ```
- **Agent Slack handle:** @{AgentName} (posts in #people as itself once qm/P3 is live)
- **Agent Notion user:** {machine user name} (every Culture tracker edit attributed to the agent, once the tracker exists)

## Operators

| Operator | Role | Owns | Email |
|---|---|---|---|
| Satyam | Founder | All never-delegated decisions across this pack: performance judgments, review content, calibration, offboarding/termination decisions, policy | {founder email} |
| {People Lead / manager, once hired} | People Lead | Day-to-day review of this agent's queues, tunes cadence config once decided | {email} |

## Escalation contacts (immediate, per `../config/playbook.md` §Immediate escalation pattern)

| Trigger | Escalate to | How |
|---|---|---|
| Exit interview surfaces harassment/discrimination/safety/legal content | Founder (or People Lead once hired) | Content-free flag to #people, transcript to the private delivery channel once gated (`../config/notion.md`) |
| Any pressure to skip a never-delegated guardrail | Founder | Refuse, note it, continue the rest of the task |

